      "excerpt": "As soon as one thinks of the word \"wildlife,\" other mammals, like squirrels or birds that are more visible to them, come to mind. However, biodiversity is much broader. Biodiversity includes anything living in this earth, ranging from plants, fungi, insects, spiders, amphibians, microorganisms, and animals.",
